          %h1#contents Contents
          .maruku_toc
            %ul
              %li
                %a{:href => "#idea"} Idea
              %li
                %a{:href => "#properties"} Properties
              %ul
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#LongSequenceInCohomology"} Long sequence in cohomology
                %li
                  %a{:href => "#InLogarithmicGeometry"} In logarithmic geometry
              %li
                %a{:href => "#related_concepts"} Related concepts
              %li
                %a{:href => "#references"} References
          %h2#idea Idea
          %p
            In the context of
            = succeed "," do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+analytic+geometry"} complex analytic geometry
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/short+exact+sequence"} short exact sequence
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 0
                  %mo →
                  %mi ker
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi exp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⟶
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔾
                    %mi a
                  %mover
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mrow
                      %mi exp
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                        %mfrac
                          %mi i
                          %mi ℏ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔾
                    %mi m
                  %mo →
                  %mn 0
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  0 \to ker(\exp) \longrightarrow \mathbb{G}_{a} \stackrel{\exp(\tfrac{i}{\hbar}(-))}{\longrightarrow} \mathbb{G}_m \to 0
          %p
            given by the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/exponential+map"} exponential map
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi exp
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                    %mfrac
                      %mi i
                      %mi ℏ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \exp(\tfrac{i}{\hbar}(-))
            from the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/additive+group"} additive group
            to the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/multiplicative+group"} multiplicative group
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℏ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \hbar
            is any element of
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℝ
                    %mo ×
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{R}^\times
            (“
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Planck%27s+constant"}> Planck's constant
            ”) but is traditionally set either to
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 1
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1
            or to
            = succeed "." do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mn 1
                    %mo{:stretchy => "false"} /
                    %mn 2
                    %mi π
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} 1/2 \pi
          %p
            Hence more explicitly over the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+numbers"} complex numbers
            this is
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 0
                  %mo →
                  %mi ℏ
                  %mn 2
                  %mi π
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo ⟶
                  %mi ℂ
                  %mover
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mrow
                      %mi exp
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                        %mfrac
                          %mi i
                          %mi ℏ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msup
                    %mi ℂ
                    %mo ×
                  %mo →
                  %mn 0
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo ,
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  0 \to \hbar2\pi\mathbb{Z} \longrightarrow \mathbb{C} \stackrel{\exp(\tfrac{i}{\hbar}(-))}{\longrightarrow} \mathbb{C}^\times \to 0
                  \\,,
          %p
            where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mi ℂ
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}
            denotes the complex numbers as the additive
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/abelian+group"} abelian group
            and where
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi ℂ
                    %mo ×
                  %mo =
                  %mi ℂ
                  %mo −
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} {
                  %mn 0
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} }
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathbb{C}^\times = \mathbb{C} - \{0\}
            is the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/group+of+units"} group of units
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/ring"} ring
            structure of the complex numbers.
          %p
            Often this is considered and displayed
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/slice+topos"} relative
            to a
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/complex+analytic+space"} complex analytic space
            = succeed "," do
              %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                %semantics
                  %mrow
                    %mi X
                  %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} X
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/structure+sheaf"} structure sheaf
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mi X
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} \mathcal{O}_{X}
            it reads
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %mn 0
                  %mo →
                  %mi Lconst
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⟶
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mi X
                  %mover
                    %mo ⟶
                    %mrow
                      %mi exp
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mstyle{:displaystyle => "false"}
                        %mfrac
                          %mi i
                          %mi ℏ
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                      %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                      %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %msubsup
                    %mi 𝒪
                    %mi X
                    %mo ×
                  %mo →
                  %mn 0
                  %mspace{:width => "thinmathspace"}
                  %mo .
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  0 \to Lconst(\mathbb{Z}) \longrightarrow \mathcal{O}_X \stackrel{\exp(\tfrac{i}{\hbar}(-))}{\longrightarrow} \mathcal{O}_X^\times \to 0
                  \\,.
          %p
            In this form the sequence is then also called the
            = succeed "." do
              %em exponential sheaf sequence
          %h2#properties Properties
          %h3#LongSequenceInCohomology Long sequence in cohomology
          %p
            The
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/connecting+homomorphisms"} connecting homomorphisms
            of the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/long+exact+sequence+in+cohomology"} long exact sequence in cohomology
            induces by the exponential exact sequence
          .maruku-equation
            %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "block", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
              %semantics
                %mrow
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mi n
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo ,
                  %msub
                    %mi 𝔾
                    %mi m
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                  %mo ⟶
                  %msup
                    %mi H
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo +
                      %mn 1
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} (
                  %mo{:lspace => "verythinmathspace", :rspace => "0em"} −
                  %mo ,
                  %mi ℤ
                  %mo{:stretchy => "false"} )
                %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"}
                  H^n(-,\mathbb{G}_m) \longrightarrow H^{n+1}(-,\mathbb{Z})
          %p
            encode the canonical
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/characteristic+classes"} characteristic classes
            of
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/line+n-bundles"} line n-bundles
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                For
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo =
                      %mn 1
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n=1
                this is the
                %a{:href => "first+Chern+class#InComplexAnalyticGeometry"} first Chern class in complex analytic geometry
                defined on the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Picard+group"} Picard group
                of
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holomorphic+line+bundles"} holomorphic line bundles
            %li
              %p
                for
                %math.maruku-mathml{:display => "inline", :xmlns => "http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML"}
                  %semantics
                    %mrow
                      %mi n
                      %mo =
                      %mn 2
                    %annotation{:encoding => "application/x-tex"} n = 2
                this is the complex analytic-analog of the
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Dixmier-Douady+class"} Dixmier-Douady class
                of
                = succeed "," do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/holomorphic+2-line+bundles"} holomorphic 2-line bundles
                = succeed ";" do
                  %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/bigger+Brauer+group"} bigger Brauer group
          %p and so on.
          %h3#InLogarithmicGeometry In logarithmic geometry
          %p
            In
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/algebraic+geometry"} algebraic geometry
            there is no exponential sequence, the closest analogs being the
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kummer+sequence"} Kummer sequence
            and the
            = succeed "." do
              %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Artin-Schreier+sequence"} Artin-Schreier sequence
            %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/logarithmic+geometry"} logarithmic geometry
            there is again a kind of exponential sequence (e.g.
            = succeed "," do
              %a{:href => "#Ogus01"} Ogus 01, chapter IV, remark 1.1.7
            = succeed ")." do
              %a{:href => "#Brylinski94"} Brylinski 94, page 15
            = succeed "." do
              %a{:href => "#KatoNakayama99"} Kato-Nakayama 99, section 1.4
          %h2#related_concepts Related concepts
          %ul
            %li
              %p
                %a.existingWikiWord{:href => "/nlab/show/Kummer+exact+sequence"} Kummer exact sequence
            %li
